& [SJS]
  + Situation: effectless lifecycle phases are valid values but no form currently tells a host exactly what operation follows an interrupted phase
  + Justification: digest-bound public checkpoints permit deterministic reentry testing without relying on a KV cache hidden state or resident process
  + Solution: compile phase-derived checkpoints and prove every phase resumes to the same independently reconstructed admitted trace

& [Delineation]
  + checkpoint serialization is not persistence
  + pure fixture resume is not process resume or provider reconnection
  + exact trace equivalence is not semantic equivalence between independent model generations
  + checkpoint local integrity precedes and cannot replace canonical transport binding

& [DataDrivenDesign]
  + next operation is a total function of four dispatch phases
  + trace digest uses a checkpoint-specific domain over deterministic compact JSON
  + each resume case retains checkpoint and both actual resumed and independently reconstructed uninterrupted traces
  + transport position and terminal flag fix case order and prevent cross-kind reuse

& [FacultyReview]
  + Honesty constrains resume and equivalence claims to deterministic fixture state
  + Security validates checkpoint integrity then exact canonical packet binding
  + Planner derives one next operation per phase and orders all cases
  + Weaver connects interrupted public state to the remaining lifecycle transforms
  + Scribe retains the checkpoint digest operation and equality witnesses
  + Refiner avoids storing duplicated instructions beyond the phase-derived next-operation handle
  + Observer compares resumed and uninterrupted traces for every legal interruption point

& [Decision]
  + activate isolated dispatch_checkpoint forms compiler local validator resume functions corpus serializer and adversarial tests
  + keep persistence provider reconnection and hidden-state recovery outside authority

& [Rollback]
  + additive module exports and tests remove without changing predecessor forms or behavior
